        },
        "instructions": "Choose one exact, fixed button sequence to advance safely using only CURRENT screenshot. Distinguish rising, falling and standing by Mario relative to visible surfaces. A fresh jump must start when standing on a solid surface, never in midair. Full jump holds last40frames; do not use them if forward travel would overshoot a small safe landing. No automatic correction exists.",
        "type": "choice"
      }
    },
    "initial_provider_text": [
      "{\"game\":\"Super Mario Bros 1-1\",\"instructions\":\"Play Mario1-1 alive to the flag on the right, using screenshots only. Current screenshot is last; game is paused while deciding. Solid surfaces support Mario; background hills are decorative. A fresh jump requires A released then pressed while Mario is standing on a solid surface. Hold A during ascent to gain height; release on descent to prepare the next jump. Holding A through landing cannot jump again. Solid overhead blocks interrupt ascent; side contact with enemies hurts, landing on them can stomp. B runs faster and farther. At a visible gap, take off from solid ground near its edge with enough forward travel to land on the far side. A fixed jump sequence chosen in midair will not restart automatically when Mario lands; use a release action to land first, then choose the next jump.\",\"next_control_interval_native_frames\":\"Choose one fixed button sequence from the action list.\",\"previous_controls\":[]}",
